{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/303482-looking-for-group-boulder-co","id":303482,"title":"Looking for Group, Boulder CO","path":["Home","Onyx Path","General","Conventions, Gatherings, and Online Play"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-11-05T11:28:48-08:00","id":303482,"title":"Looking for Group, Boulder CO","content":"My wife and I are adult, experienced roleplayers (early 30's) and are looking for gaming in Boulder, CO.<br /> <br /> I do have a good deal of Storytelling experience but we'd really like to play together again, it's been three years since our last ongoing game and that's just too long.<br /> <br /> We're huge WoD fans and actually met on the old White Wolf forum, we're open to most any sort of game, preferring the classic storylines but okay trying the new.<br /> <br /> As players we do our best to be generous to the storyteller and true to our characters, and are far more interested in character growth and fun than being some bizarrely overpowered character.<br /> <br /> We love White Wolf but if you know of another system game ongoing we're open to that as well. Open to any questions, comments, suggestions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4243-zensparkle","name":"ZenSparkle","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-05T12:05:05-08:00","id":303571,"title":"","content":"Have you thought about playing something online? Skype or Google Hangouts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-05T18:45:59-08:00","id":303985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/303482-looking-for-group-boulder-co?p=303571#post303571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have you thought about playing something online? Skype or Google Hangouts?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's a possibility, but my wife does web design and we're hoping for some social time that doesn't include staring at a screen. If nothing pans out we will likely give it a try though, thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4243-zensparkle","name":"ZenSparkle","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-13T12:37:28-08:00","id":311518,"title":"","content":"I recently moved from Colorado and though I don't know of any current White Wolf games there, I can recommend a few places to look. <br /> <br /> Karliquin's in Boulder has a bulletin board that you could post on. Karl who runs the store is a nice guy. <a href=\"http://karliquin.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://karliquin.com/</a><br /> <br /> Total Escape Games in Broomfield is a really classy store. It's not as close as Karliquin's, but is definitely worth checking out. They have a bulletin board, too. Steve, the owner, is another great guy. <a href=\"http://totalescapegames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://totalescapegames.com/</a><br /> <br /> Hobbytown USA in Westminster doesn't have a huge selection of games, but the guy who runs the games department, Edward, is a Vampire player. He may be able to hook you up with a game. <a href=\"http://www.hobbiescolorado.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.hobbiescolorado.com/</a><br /> <br /> Local conventions have always been a good way for me to meet gamers. The biggest gaming cons are Genghis Con and Tacticon. They are organized by a group of volunteers known as the Denver Gamers Association. In the past, there has not been a lot of White Wolf games run at their cons, but there are normally a few at each convention. <a href=\"http://denvergamers.org/\" target=\"_blank\">http://denvergamers.org/</a><br /> <br /> There is a Meetup group called The Denver RPG Group. The people who run it and most of the people in it are great and play good, story driven games. <a href=\"http://www.meetup.com/Denver-RPG/\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.meetup.com/Denver-RPG/</a><br /> <br /> Lastly, I highly encourage you to check out Black and Read in Arvada. They also have a bulletin board (of sorts, people post fliers around the magazines), but what you really have to check out is their selection of games. They have a HUGE selection of new and used White Wolf books. Unless things have changed since I left, it's a White Wolf players paradise. <a href=\"http://www.blackandread.net/site/\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.blackandread.net/site/</a><br /> <br /> I hope that helps! Good luck finding a game!<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3306-longshanks","name":"longshanks","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}